@@ -1,35 +0,0 @@
-# Constellation Commander v0.3 Windows Companion
-
-The Windows companion makes **Normal Chat mode** the default. It starts and supervises a loopback-only Commander bridge at `127.0.0.1:47721`, monitors browser-companion presence, starts with Windows, and keeps the hosted Remote-MCP transport in an optional Advanced section.
-
-## First run
-
-Run `INSTALL-COMPANION.cmd`.
-
-The installer copies the complete bundle to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ConstellationCommander` and starts `ConstellationCommander.exe --first-run`. The app then:
-
-1. enables Start with Windows;
-2. starts the bundled Commander bridge and waits for a real `/health` response;
-3. opens the bundled `browser-companion` folder and copies its path;
-4. opens `chrome://extensions/` when Chrome is available;
-5. waits for the browser companion heartbeat and reports **Connected — ready for normal chats**.
-
-Chrome itself requires the one-time **Load unpacked** trust action for an off-store development extension. Commander does not bypass that browser security decision. After the extension is trusted once, normal operation is automatic.
-
-## Bundle contents
-
-- `ConstellationCommander.exe` — self-contained .NET 8 WinForms manager
-- `runtime/node.exe` — bundled Node runtime
-- `agent/` — local executor, bridge, and optional remote-device client
-- `browser-companion/` — Manifest V3 ChatGPT companion
-- `INSTALL-COMPANION.cmd` — per-user install helper
-
-## Controls
-
-- **Connect Browser** — reopens the one-time Chrome setup/repair flow.
-- **Test** — verifies the live bridge and browser-companion heartbeat.
-- **Data Folder** — opens Commander local state.
-- **Start with Windows** — controls per-user autostart.
-- **Advanced — hosted directory-plugin transport** — optional stable HTTPS relay/device connection; not required for normal browser chats.
-
-No OpenAI API key is required by Normal Chat mode and the app does not hand local work to ChatGPT Work.
